        "like": 1
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "One workaround for this is filling the VRCStation's animator slot with a different animation controller from the Avatar SDK, but this fix is very easy to break at runtime and may be degrading in efficacy over time. (Also, behaviors may be completely different if the station has script-controlled exit!)\n\nGenerally, the rule is that the avatar *absolutely must* have an AFK state in the animator in order to unlock FBT while in-station even if the alternate animator trick is used - assuming it still works (at the time of this writing). \n\nUsually this isn't an issue because many users never even touch their locomotion animation controller, much less remove a piece of it. But because the tools that make modifications on this are very widespread (and released despite incompatibility with stations), there are many avatars using these tools that cannot unlock for FBT at all.\n\nAvatars without an AFK state or which have had the AFK state disabled /at time of world load/, or which use some specific newer (at the time of writing) versions of GoGoLoCo may be completely incapable of unlocking in stations even if the user is in FBT. There is no workaround for this case.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-08-01T20:23:41.973Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The recent scaling update partially fixed a bug that allowed a player to use full body tracking while in a seat/station through reloading the avatar. It's currently still possible through entering and exiting the afk animation, but it's still a bug and may get fixed in the future. \n\n It was useful for better positioning your avatar in vehicles and seats on avatars or to use more dynamic poses than what the station offers by default. It's a rather niche usecase but allows for some neat creative moments. \n\nIt would be nice to have this as an option that contextually appears in the quick action menu for fbt users who are in a station which disables the station animation for the user when activated.\n\nEdit: added a picture as an example. It's not a really good example but it wouldn't have been possible to reposition and pose for that pucture without the fbt station bug as it was taken mid-flight where a seat is needed to be attached to the aircraft.",
